4. ORDERED-PAIR/EDGE SECTORS AND S217 RESIDUES
   ordered-pair sector deck mode=size    : separates 55/56 classes
   ordered-pair sector deck mode=internal: separates 55/56 classes
   ordered-pair sector deck mode=cross   : separates 56/56 classes
   ordered-pair sector deck mode=full    : separates 56/56 classes
   C3 histogram over all U(6): {0: 1, 1: 4, 2: 4, 3: 4, 4: 10, 5: 8, 6: 12, 7: 8, 8: 5}
   C3 histogram over SC(6):   {0: 1, 2: 2, 4: 2, 6: 4, 8: 3}
   S217 local line law: K_{k,k+1} has k(k+1) lines, rank 2k, rectangle residue rank k(k-1).
   For k=4 this residue rank is 12; for n=6 global rectangle/hourglass redundancy is 26.
   Reading: ordered-pair cross sectors and S217 rectangle/hourglass cycles are the same kind of cut payload: a mixed coordinate killed by a scalar shadow but recoverable as a sidecar.

5. OBSERVER-EXTENSION / CUT PAYLOAD ABSTRACT
   Data form:
     base quotient Q, observer/cut word sigma, stabilizer Aut(Q),
     sidecar C(sigma), sink map Phi(Q,sigma), and legality exit.
   Controlled-forgetting recurrence:
     retained_{r+1} = (retained_r, C_r) / Aut(retained_r)
     debt_r = kernel(C_r -> LRC predicate)
     allow forgetting only if debt_r is reconstructed, annihilated,
     descended to a smaller family, AP/GW equality, or named residual debt.

   Applications across this repo:
   problem                         retained shadow                    hidden payload
   A000568/rooted perspective     rooted node type                   new observer incident word and cross-sector chirality
     sidecar=ordered-pair sector deck / edge tail-tip sector word; exit=exact finite first-failure audit
   LRC threshold packet           safe/open status near a boundary phase endpoint owner, period deck, route label
     sidecar=labelled packet sheaf with hidden-coordinate ledger; exit=HYP-3039/HYP-3043 controlled-forgetting protocol
   Residual capacitor cuts        mixed route pair survives coarse boundary type which generator/cut class blocks it
     sidecar=finite min-cut payload plus owner strip; exit=pair-good decoy repair and capacitor first-cut IDs
   Haar drop/add square           row/column margin shadow           mixed zeta T00-T01-T10+T11
     sidecar=rectangle product residue; exit=exact zeta sign or dual annihilation
   S217 fixed-path diagonal flow  line-count or half-tiling shadow   rectangle/hourglass cycle residue
     sidecar=GF(2) cut-space basis on K_{k,k+1}; exit=sidecar admissibility; not a scalar count
   Matrix sidecar observability   rank/spectrum/scalar invariant     hidden coordinate separating route/status fibers
     sidecar=observability matrix column; exit=separate, reconstruct, annihilate, descend, or name debt
   Moser/fibbinary automata       regular-language membership        scale, parity-position, carry boundary
     sidecar=automaton state plus valuation/topology sidecar; exit=automatic telemetry before LRC handoff
   Perfect-number/divisor lane    abundancy or Euler-product scalar  prime-power lane and divisor-lattice fiber
     sidecar=divisor-lattice/SNF payload; exit=squarefree blindness repair
   Fixed-path tournament atlas    Hamiltonian-path presentation      fiber H(T)/Aut(T) and path-reversal branch data
     sidecar=presentation-fiber payload; exit=unrooted class quotient only after fiber audit
   Proof-obligation automaton     coarse theorem stage               which obligation remains after a quotient
     sidecar=named residual state plus legal exit; exit=agent coordination and next lemma target

